P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F.F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50"},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-011502","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"RC1","Cell_line":"HepG2","Time(h)":48,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":">200","IC50_Dark_value":200,"IC50_Light(M*10^-6)":">200","IC50_Light_value":200,"Excitation_Wavelength(nm)":460,"Irradiation_Time(minutes)":60,"Irradiation_Power(W*m^-2)":19.53,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1016/j.molstruc.2024.138997","Year":2024,"Counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F.F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","Type":"IC50"}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"RC1","value":-2.81,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1016/j.molstruc.2024.138997","year":2024,"counterion":"[Cl-].[Cl-]","record_id":"MLDB-000639","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The partition coefficients of three complexes were measured by the “shake-flask” method [39]. The chloride salts of Ru(II) complexes (200 μM) were dissolved in water saturated with n-octanol and an equal volume of n-octanol saturated with water. The mixture was shaken for 24 h at room temperature. The concentrations of the complexes in the oil and water phases were determined using absorption spectra at the MLCT band."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":2,"value":0.3,"value_relation":"=","std":0.2,"type_authors":"logD","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"PBS","doi":"10.1021/jacs.9b13620","year":2020,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F.F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-000971","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipophilicity of a complex was determined by measuring its distribution coefficient between the PBS and Octanol phase by using the “shake-flask” method. For this technique, the used phases were previously saturated in each other. The complex was dissolved in the phase (A) with its major presence with an absorbance of about 0.5 at 450 nm. This solution was then mixed with an equal volume of the other phase (B) at 80 rpm for 8 h with an Invitrogen sample mixer and then equilibrated overnight. The phase A was then carefully separated from phase B. The amount of the complex before and after the sample mixing was determined by UV/Vis spectroscopy at 450 nm using a SpectraMax M2 Microplate Reader (Molecular Devices). The evaluation of the complexes was repeated three times and the ratio between the organic and aqueous phase calculated."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"[Ru(phen)2(Me2bpy)]2+","value":-2.9,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1039/c4dt02139h","year":2014,"counterion":"[Cl-].[Cl-]","record_id":"MLDB-005029","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The octanol-water partition coefficients were determined by the shake-flask technique: each ruthenium complex (at 0.1 mM) was dissolved in the water phase and an equal volume of n-octanol was added. The two phases were mutually saturated by shaking overnight at ambient temperature and then were allowed to separate on standing. The concentration of the metal complex in each phase was determined spectrophotometrically at lambda = 450 nm."}],"ccdc":["QUFGEG"]}